                    136.0,
                    946.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Table 2: UCI energy-efficiency benchmark (Tsanas & Xifara, 2012): mean test  $ R^{2} $ on the 80/20 hold-out and approximate parameter count, for the two decoupled tbtree configurations (coskewness / combined split, covariance leaves) and the black-box references. The combined-split tbtree is the best single-tree model and matches the black-box regressors to within noise at a fraction of their size. Best single tree in bold.</div>\n",
